  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a permutation PPP of the integers [1,N][1, N][1,N].\n\nPerform the following operation sequence:\n\n\nFor integers i=1,2,...Ni = 1, 2, ...Ni=1,2,...N (in this order), perform one of the following actions:\n\nChoose an integer XXX such that 1≤X&lt;N1 \\le X &lt; N1≤X&lt;N, and either PX=iP_X = iPX​=i or PX+1=iP_{X + 1} = iPX+1​=i, then swap PXP_XPX​ and PX+1P_{X + 1}PX+1​.\nChoose to do nothing.\n\n\nLet f(P)f(P)f(P) denote the lexicographically smallest permutation possible after the above operation sequence.\n\nYou are given a permutation PPP of the integers [1,N][1, N][1,N].\n\nFind f(P)f(P)f(P).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the size of the permutation PPP\nThe next line contains NNN integers - P1,P2,...,PNP_1, P_2, ..., P_NP1​,P2​,...,PN​\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print the lexicographically smallest permutation possible with the operation sequence from PPP, i.e. F(P)F(P)F(P).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Pi≤N1 \\le P_i \\le N1≤Pi​≤N",
      "Pi≠PjP_i \\ne P_jPi​=Pj​ for i≠ji \\ne ji=j",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
