        "input": "5\n3\n1 3 2\n3\n3 2 1\n4\n2 4 3 1\n5\n1 4 2 3 5\n1\n1",
        "output": "1 2 3 \n1 3 2 \n2 1 4 3 \n1 2 3 4 5 \n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : Here is the required operation sequence to obtain [1,2,3][1, 2, 3][1,2,3]:\n\ni=1i = 1i=1 : Choose to do nothing\ni=2i = 2i=2 : Choose to do nothing\ni=3i = 3i=3 : Swap P2P_2P2​ and P3P_3P3​ (P2=3P_2 = 3P2​=3 before the swap, so it is valid). PPP becomes [1,2,3][1, 2, 3][1,2,3].\n\nTest Case 2 : It can be shown that lexicographically smaller permutations than [1,3,2][1, 3, 2][1,3,2] are not possible. Here is how to obtain [1,3,2][1, 3, 2][1,3,2]:\n\ni=1i = 1i=1 : Swap P2P_2P2​ and P3P_3P3​ (P3=1P_3 = 1P3​=1 before the swap so it is valid). PPP becomes [3,1,2][3, 1, 2][3,1,2].\ni=2i = 2i=2 : Choose to do nothing\ni=3i = 3i=3 : Swap P1P_1P1​ and P2P_2P2​ (P1=3P_1 = 3P1​=3 before the swap, so it is valid). PPP becomes [1,3,2][1, 3, 2][1,3,2]."
